planningNotes.approachesConsidered:
(1) Drive-type refusal: refuse every subst or remote drive letter, using QueryDosDevice/GetDriveType through JNA. It is cheap and never reads a share. Rejected because:
- DoD 1 requires an unrelated folder on the same subst drive to stay on PATH;
- it adds native calls (the plugin uses no JNA today);
- a benign mapped home drive would be dropped.
(2) Resolve the drive letter the way Node does, through GetFinalPathNameByHandle via JNA. That is VS Code parity, but it is native code with handle management. Rejected for the same reasons.
(3) Identity through Files.isSameFile over the real path's ancestors (chosen):
- pure NIO;
- the probe showed it true for subst, volume-GUID and loopback-UNC spellings of the same folder;
- it catches the reverse case, a project opened through a subst letter;
- it fails closed on unknown drives.
(4) Skip identity on the project's own drive letter, as an optimization. Rejected: walking every candidate is simpler and strictly safer, and the cost is small (O(depth) per entry, once per spawn or selection).

