Helper withSubst(target: File, body: (String) -> T): T
- For letters 'Z' downTo 'D':
  - Skip a letter where File("$L:\\").exists().
  - Otherwise run `File(System.getenv("SystemRoot"), "System32\\subst.exe").path`, "$L:", target.path through ProcessBuilder (redirectErrorStream; read all output, then waitFor, as junction() does).
  - On exit 0: try { return body("$L:") } finally { run subst "$L:" /D }.
  - A nonzero exit means the letter was taken or is held by a remembered network mapping: try the next letter.
- Call `/D` only for a drive this helper created; never touch a pre-existing mapping.
- If no letter works: assumeTrue("no free drive letter for subst", false).
- Error handling: a cleanup failure must not hide the body's own failure.

N-row: a subst drive into the project is inside it by identity. Setup:
- work = newFolder("work");
- project = File(work, "proj"), with bin/ created;
- other = File(work, "other"), created;
- outsideA = newFolder("path-a").
Shape 1, withSubst(project) { d ->
- isOutsideProject("$d\\", project.path) is false (the drive root is the project);
- "$d\\bin" is false;
- "$d\\missing" is false (a missing folder: its parent, the root, is the project). }
Shape 2, withSubst(work) { d ->
- "$d\\proj" and "$d\\proj\\bin" are false: the drive is substed to the parent and the entry reaches the project;
- "$d\\other" is TRUE: an unrelated folder on the same subst drive is kept;
- reverse alias: isOutsideProject(File(project, "bin").path, "$d\\proj") is false, for a project opened through the subst drive;
- PATH: supervisorFor(project, { null }, { null }).protectedDaemonEnvironment(env, project.path), with PATH = outsideA, "$d\\proj", "$d\\proj\\bin", "$d\\other". Then assertEquals(mapOf("PATH" to listOf(outsideA.path, "$d\\other").joinToString(File.pathSeparator)), env). }
After both shapes, the drive is gone: an entry on that now-free letter ("$d\\bin") answers false, because no existing folder proves anything.
Controls: outsideA.path is true and project.path is false, so each refusal comes from identity alone.

